01:01:06,666 --> 01:01:12,666
Two Lovers is a 2008 American romantic drama film, directed by James Gray, and
starring Joaquin Phoenix, Gwyneth Paltrow, and Vinessa Shaw.

11
01:07:13,333 --> 01:07:19,333
The film takes its inspiration from Fyodor Dostoyevsky's 1848 short story "White Nights", which had already
been turned into a film seven times, first by Luchino Visconti: Le Notti Bianche (1957).

12
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
It is set in the largely Russian Jewish neighborhood Brighton Beach in
New York City, as was Gray's first film Little Odessa.

13
01:19:26,666 --> 01:19:32,666
Two Lovers premiered in competition at the 2008 Cannes Film Festival in May.

14
01:25:33,333 --> 01:25:39,333
The film was Gray's third to enter the competition at this festival.

15
01:31:40,000 --> 01:31:46,000
It was released on February 13, 2009.

16
01:37:46,666 --> 01:37:52,666
The film explores themes of new year's eve, new york city, love
of one's life, neighbor, brooklyn, new york city.

17
01:43:53,333 --> 01:43:59,333
The tone is emotional.
